course: dictionary
lesson: 22
title: Absolute: total and certain
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Absolute means total, complete, or as much as possible. The Rat says, «there is nothing—absolute nothing—half so much worth doing as simply messing about in boats». The dash and the word absolute tell you he means nothing at all, not even a little.
explain: Absolute can also mean certain and not changing, like an absolute rule. In everyday talk people use it to make a word stronger, so the Harrogate week was «absolute chaos». Chaos is already big, and absolute makes it even bigger.
explain: Maths and science use absolute in exact ways. The absolute value of −5 is 5, its distance from zero. Absolute zero is the coldest temperature possible. Read the words near absolute to see which meaning fits.
fact: Absolute means total, complete, or as much as possible.
fact: «Absolute silence» means complete silence, with no sound at all.
fact: An absolute rule is one that is certain and does not change.
fact: The absolute value of a number is its distance from zero, and it is always positive or zero.
fact: «Absolute chaos» is an informal way to say total mess, and it is used to make a word stronger.
exercise: «The Harrogate week was absolute chaos.» What does absolute mean here? | Something to do with boats | Slightly messy | *Complete, total chaos | Calm and peaceful
exercise: In maths, what is the absolute value of −5? | *5 | 10 | −10 | −5
exercise: The Rat says «nothing—absolute nothing». What does absolute tell you? | Something that is wet | *Nothing at all, not even a little | Something that is only sometimes true | Something very small
test: In science, absolute zero is the coldest possible temperature. What does absolute suggest here? | Hidden under ice | Warm and cosy | Changing all the time | *The lowest possible, with no limit below it
test: «The king was an absolute ruler.» What does this mean? | A ruler who is slightly bent | A ruler with a small wooden stick | A ruler who is always late | *A ruler with complete power
exam: Which meaning of absolute is used in «an absolute rule»? | Distance from zero | *Certain and not changing | Total silence | A kind of boat
